ask(c,'In the two-link drawing, what do the downward m₁g and m₂g arrows represent?', ['The gravitational forces on the two links','The commanded joint torques τ₁ and τ₂','The angular velocity vectors of the two joints','The Coriolis forces for every possible motion'],['The arrows are masses multiplied by downward gravitational acceleration.','Joint torques are the separate curved arrows.','Angular velocities are not labeled m times g.','Coriolis effects depend on motion and are labeled separately.'],kind='diagram')
ask(c,'For two revolute joints, M=[[2,1],[1,3]] kg·m², q̈=(1,0) rad/s² and V=G=F=0. What torque vector is required?', ['(2,1) N·m','(2,0) N·m','(1,3) N·m','(3,4) N·m'],['Multiplication by the first matrix column gives (2,1), including coupling torque at joint 2.','This ignores the off-diagonal inertia.','This selects the second column rather than the first.','This assumes both accelerations equal one.'],kind='numerical',formula=[DYN],pages=[729,730],steps=['Compute Mq̈=(2×1+1×0,1×1+3×0).','The result is (2,1) N·m; all other torque terms are zero.'])
ask(c,'At a static pose with zero joint velocity and acceleration, which term may still be nonzero even if friction is neglected?', ['G(q), the gravity torque','Mq̈, the inertial acceleration torque','V(q,0), the ordinary Coriolis/centrifugal torque','The velocity error solely because q̇ is zero'],['Gravity depends on pose and can require holding torque at rest.','The stipulated zero acceleration makes this product zero.','The standard velocity-quadratic rigid-body terms vanish at zero velocity.','Velocity error depends on desired velocity too; zero actual velocity alone does not imply an error.'],assumptions=['Ordinary rigid-body V consists of velocity-quadratic Coriolis/centrifugal terms; F is neglected.'])
c=concept(730,'Partitioned inverse-dynamics controller','Model scaling, additive cancellation, virtual-command meaning and physical torque.')
ask(c,'Which choice realizes the lecture’s exact partitioned controller τ=ατ′+β?', ['α=M; β=V+G+F','α=M⁻¹; β=V+G+F','α=I; β=M+V+G+F','α=M; β=−V−G−F'],['The plant requires M times commanded acceleration plus the additive loads.','Using inverse inertia does not reconstruct the required actuator torque.','A matrix M cannot be added directly to torque vectors, and this omits inertia scaling.','Negative compensation doubles rather than cancels the plant’s load terms under this convention.'],formula=[DYN],pages=[730,731])
