ask(c,'If q_d=0.8 rad and q=1.0 rad, which error and proportional virtual-acceleration contribution result for K_p=25 s⁻²?', ['E=−0.2 rad and K_pE=−5 rad/s²','E=+0.2 rad and K_pE=+5 rad/s²','E=−0.2 rad and K_pE=−0.008 rad/s²','E=−1.8 rad and K_pE=−45 rad/s²'],['Desired minus actual is −0.2, multiplied by 25 to oppose the overshoot.','This reverses the defined error sign.','This divides by the gain.','This adds the angles before applying a negative sign.'],kind='numerical',formula=[ERR],steps=['E=0.8−1.0=−0.2 rad.','K_pE=25(−0.2)=−5 rad/s².'])
ask(c,'Which condition makes the displayed vector error equation split into the stated independent scalar equations in the original joint coordinates?', ['K_p and K_v are diagonal in those coordinates','Only M must be diagonal before cancellation','Only the desired joint positions must be constant','Every diagonal entry of K_p must equal every entry of K_v'],['Diagonal gains prevent feedback cross-terms between the error components after exact dynamic cancellation.','Exact inverse dynamics can cancel a coupled M; diagonal gains are still needed for the displayed scalar form.','A constant reference does not remove off-diagonal gains.','The two gains have different units and need not be numerically equal.'],difficulty='medium',formula=[ERR],pages=[730,731])
ask(c,'For ë+6ė+9e=0 with time in seconds, which characteristic roots and damping type apply?', ['A repeated root −3 s⁻¹; critical damping','Roots ±3 s⁻¹; one unstable mode','Roots −6±3i s⁻¹; underdamping','A repeated root +3 s⁻¹; unstable response'],['s²+6s+9=(s+3)².','This would follow from s²−9, not the given polynomial.','Those roots do not satisfy the given coefficients.','The linear coefficient is positive, so the repeated root is negative.'],kind='numerical',formula=[ERR],steps=['Substitute e=e₀ exp(st) into the homogeneous equation.','Factor s²+6s+9=(s+3)².','The repeated negative real root is critical damping.'])
