ask(c,'Which set contains the three ideal assumptions explicitly listed for nonlinear control?', ['Continuous computation, exact model knowledge, no sensing/actuation delay','Discrete computation, uncertain model knowledge, no feedback','Continuous computation, diagonal inertia, no gravitational force','Exact model knowledge, zero joint velocity, constant payload torque only'],['These are the slide’s continuous-time, model-accuracy and delay assumptions.','These describe practical limitations rather than the ideal assumptions.','Diagonal inertia and zero gravity are not required for full computed torque.','Zero motion and a special payload torque are not stated requirements.'],kind='statement')
ask(c,'After a tool change, tracking worsens even though the servo period is unchanged. Which listed issue is directly implicated?', ['Model inaccuracy from changed load parameters','A mathematically necessary decrease in sampling frequency','The disappearance of all gravity terms','Conversion of the controller into an open-loop system'],['A different payload can change mass, inertia and gravity loads while computation timing remains fixed.','The scenario explicitly holds the sampling period fixed.','Changing payload does not remove gravity.','The feedback architecture can remain unchanged.'],kind='scenario')
